    isbefore: []  # 063b
    duplicate_of: []  # 063b
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 063b
    pr_ref:  # 063b
    description: "The residual half of INV-rahib after the post-merge boundary fix.\n\nOwner ruling 2026-08-03 (pinned in tests/test_autopr_rahib_convergence.py,\nsection \"The declared terminal-state vocabulary\") replaced the invariant's\noriginal \"merged or explicit failure, no third state\" wording with a DECLARED\nCLOSED SET of terminal states, in which `unknown` -- the initializer -- IS the\nviolation signal.\n\nMEASURED, not inferred. Reading .git/AUTOPR_HISTORY.jsonl (481 invocations,\n2026-08-03 -> 2026-09-16):\n\n    final_state              exit    n\n    merged                      0  359\n    ci_failed                   1   49\n    merged                      1   41   <- fixed by the post-merge boundary\n    unknown                     1   13   <- THIS ITEM\n    failed_merge                1    9\n    push_rejected_diverged      1    5\n    governance_pending          0    3\n    unknown                     0    1   <- THIS ITEM, worst case\n    queued_vpr                  0    1\n\n14 of 481 (2.9%) ended in no declared terminal state. Most recent 2026-09-11,\nso this is live, not historical. Nine of the 14 carry pr_number=null (died\nbefore PR creation); five carry a pr_number with merged_sha=null.\n\nThe exit-0 row (2026-08-17T08:09:02Z, PR 390, merged_sha=null) is the more\nserious shape: a run that reported SUCCESS while recording no terminal state\nand no merge. The PR numbering skips 390->394 with no `merged` row in between.\n\nMECHANISM, partly identified. `set -euo pipefail` means any unguarded command\nfailing before a state assignment aborts with the initializer still in place.\nOne confirmed contributor was fixed alongside the boundary work: gov_cleanup\nset `_autopr_state_final=\"merged\"` AFTER `cleanup_local`, so a cleanup abort\nlanded on `unknown` rather than `merged`. That accounts for the shape (pr_number\nset, merged_sha null) but has not been shown to account for all five.\n\nREFUTED HYPOTHESIS, recorded so it is not re-tried: the WI-sidot\nstderr-swallowing bug (`exec {FD}>>\"$f\" 2>/dev/null` applying the redirect\npermanently) produces exactly this signature -- an abort with empty stdout AND\nstderr. But it existed only between commits 27b46fd2ee and 8b166291a7, both on\n2026-09-15, while these rows span 2026-08-11 onward. It is not the cause.\n\nWHAT WOULD CLOSE THIS\n  (a) Enumerate the unguarded abort sites in do_pr/flush_queue that precede a\n      state assignment, the way the post-merge tail was enumerated.\n  (b) Make an undeclared abort SELF-REPORTING rather than silent: when\n      _autopr_finalize fires with the state still `unknown`, say so loudly on\n      stderr and name it as a convergence violation. Today it writes a ledger\n      row nobody reads and prints nothing.\n  (c) Re-measure the ledger after (a)/(b) and show the unknown count at 0 over\n      a comparable number of invocations.\n\nKNOWN ADJACENT, not in scope here: `auto-pr --squash` reads a confirmation\nprompt (auto-pr flag parsing) with no tty guard, so a non-interactive --squash\ndies at EOF with exit 1. It is BEFORE the trap is installed, so it writes no\nledger row at all -- invisible to this measurement rather than counted in it."  # 063b
    fields: {}  # 063b
