- op: discuss  # 9823
  at: '2026-09-16T04:47:48Z'  # 9823
  by: agent  # 9823
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 9823
  clock: 7  # 9823
  nonce: '9823'  # 9823
  message: "Filed row closed. Both halves of the mechanism addressed, with behavioral evidence.\n\n(a) ENUMERATED. Ten deliberate exits in do_pr/flush_queue were reached with\n_autopr_state_final still at its \"unknown\" initializer: the branch-ownership\nguards before both amend paths, both re-push failures and both PR lookups in\nstuck-CI recovery, the simulated outage, and the unresolvable / non-linear vPR\nqueue checks. Each now declares what it decided. Four new states join the\ndeclared closed set (failed_branch_ownership, failed_repush,\nfailed_queue_unresolvable, failed_queue_not_linear); the existing bidirectional\nvocabulary check covers them.\n\nThe enumeration is a DOMINANCE analysis, not proximity. The assignment at\nauto-pr:2085 is in the `if _pre_scenario_b_gate` arm while the exits at\n2105/2114 are in the `else` arm, so \"is there an assignment earlier in this\nfunction\" clears them -- and a 25-line distance threshold hid 2105 outright\nduring the investigation. test_no_action_path_exit_leaves_the_state_undeclared\nwalks back from each exit treating else/elif at the current level as leaving the\nconditional, and carries a two-armed fixture so neither an always-empty scanner\nnor an always-flagging one can pass it.\n\n(b) SELF-REPORTING. The remaining cause -- a set -e abort at any unguarded\ncommand -- is not statically enumerable in a 700-line function, so the run\nattributes itself. auto-pr runs under errtrace with an ERR trap recording\nfile:line and the command; _autopr_finalize prints a CONVERGENCE VIOLATION\nbanner and persists abort_site / abort_command to the sentinel and the ledger.\n\n-E is load-bearing: without it an ERR trap is not inherited by shell functions,\nand every real auto-pr abort is inside a helper. My first version of the\nbehavioral test passed with -E removed, because its fixture aborted in the same\nframe that installed the trap -- the harness contaminating its own control. Now\npinned by test_an_abort_inside_a_helper_function_is_attributed_too, verified by\nmutation (removing -E turns it red).\n\nNAMED GAPS, disclosed rather than counted as zero. A set -u unbound variable\ndoes not fire ERR (bash raises it as an expansion error, not a command failure)\nand neither does a bare exit, so an instrumented run can still record no site.\naudit-autopr-convergence therefore reports THREE states, not two: a recorded\nsite (tallied, since two runs at the same line are one bug), \"not recorded\" (the\ntrap could not see it), and \"not instrumented\" (the row has no abort_site key\nbecause it predates this change). A null default would have merged the last two\nand reported the whole historical backlog as live instrument failures.\n\nSAFETY. BASH_COMMAND holds source text, not expansion, so a line carrying\n$HG_GITHUB_TOKEN records the name. Pinned by\ntest_a_recorded_command_never_expands_a_secret rather than asserted in a comment.\n\nEVIDENCE: 10 new tests in tests/test_autopr_nazoj_undeclared_state.py driving\nthe real extracted functions under production shell flags (read from auto-pr,\nnot copied -- the previous hardcoded copy would have gone stale the moment -E\nlanded, which is the same defect that blinded test_autopr_branch_cleanup.py for\nsix weeks). 4 new tests in tests/test_audit_autopr_convergence.py. 259 passed\nacross the auto-pr + forge surface; 312 passed in a minimal venv built the way\nthe forge-arms CI job builds one. Live ledger now reports all 14 historical\nundeclared rows as \"not instrumented\" rather than as instrument failures.\n\nNOT DONE, filed separately: criterion (c), re-measuring the ledger over a\ncomparable number of post-instrumentation invocations. 485 rows took six weeks;\nthat measurement cannot be produced in the session that ships the fix. Closing\non the filed row and filing the residual, per the standing owner ruling."  # 9823
